1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
<font color="#FF8000">{\an8}Downloaded From MoviesMod.Org</font>

2
00:00:02,188 --> 00:00:04,188
-  <i>The stories</i>

3
00:00:04,188 --> 00:00:06,813
<i>that I have told you
about Greek gods</i>

4
00:00:06,813 --> 00:00:09,230
<i>and heroes and monsters, they are real.</i>

5
00:00:09,521 --> 00:00:10,896
<i>You are a half-blood,</i>

6
00:00:11,438 --> 00:00:14,480
and half-bloods are not safe
in the world.

7
00:00:15,021 --> 00:00:20,021
<i>They reach a certain age, and they begin
to understand what they are.</i>

8
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:22,563
<i>Terrible forces are driven</i>

9
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:24,438
<i>to harm them before they can become
strong enough</i>

10
00:00:24,605 --> 00:00:25,646
<i>- to fight back.</i>

11
00:00:26,188 --> 00:00:29,105
Don't worry, Mrs. Jackson.
Percy will be totally safe at camp--

12
00:00:29,105 --> 00:00:30,605
- Swear it.
- I swear.

13
00:00:32,355 --> 00:00:33,730
Mom!

14
00:00:41,438 --> 00:00:45,980
Welcome to camp, Percy Jackson.
We've been expecting you.

15
00:01:06,188 --> 00:01:07,271
Where am I?

16
00:01:09,313 --> 00:01:10,938
You drool when you sleep.

17
00:01:12,230 --> 00:01:13,230
Huh?

18
00:01:30,563 --> 00:01:33,271
It's okay. You're safe.

19
00:01:42,105 --> 00:01:43,146
It really happened.

20
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:46,855
Well, it's a big deal
to kill a monster like that.

21
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:48,730
- So, I wanted everyone to know--
- Did you see it?

22
00:01:50,521 --> 00:01:52,021
Did you see what happened to my mom?

23
00:01:52,938 --> 00:01:53,938
I did.

24
00:01:55,688 --> 00:01:56,688
I'm sorry...

25
00:01:57,313 --> 00:01:58,355
for...

26
00:02:00,146 --> 00:02:01,146
everything.

27
00:02:02,688 --> 00:02:05,271
My job was to protect you,
to get you here safely.

28
00:02:06,688 --> 00:02:08,521
Maybe if I'd told you the truth
a little sooner,

29
00:02:08,521 --> 00:02:09,980
- your mom would still be here--
- Please...

30
00:02:11,355 --> 00:02:12,396
stop.

31
00:02:13,271 --> 00:02:15,355
I know this isn't easy
but I wanna talk about it.

32
00:02:15,355 --> 00:02:16,438
I don't.

33
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:24,063
Your job was to get me here alive.

34
00:02:25,271 --> 00:02:26,438
So your job is done.

35
00:02:29,646 --> 00:02:30,646
Where are you going?

36
00:02:34,271 --> 00:02:36,813
It was so important I get here
'cause my father's a god.

37
00:02:38,563 --> 00:02:39,646
So I'm gonna go find him.

38
00:02:42,313 --> 00:02:44,980
Yeah, but it isn't that... simple.

39
00:03:20,146 --> 00:03:23,605
Excuse me?
I'm Percy Jackson, I'm new here.

40
00:03:25,730 --> 00:03:27,813
Peter Johnson is here!

41
00:03:28,688 --> 00:03:32,146
'Kay. That isn't... really my name.

42
00:03:32,646 --> 00:03:34,438
I guess I'm looking for the office?

43
00:03:34,438 --> 00:03:37,396
- Or whoever's in charge, so...
-  Wait, wait. Wait, wait, wait.

44
00:03:37,521 --> 00:03:39,396
Wait, wait, wait. Percy, um,

45
00:03:40,271 --> 00:03:42,646
Mr. D, Camp Director.

46
00:03:43,146 --> 00:03:45,063
Mr. D, this is, uh, Percy Jackson.

47
00:03:45,313 --> 00:03:47,271
Yeah, Grover. I heard him the first time.

48
00:03:47,438 --> 00:03:48,896
- Yeah. But did you?
- Okay.

49
00:03:49,313 --> 00:03:51,230
You really don't wanna start
with this guy.

50
00:03:51,688 --> 00:03:53,188
- He's starting with me.
- Percy,

51
00:03:53,605 --> 00:03:55,563
the D is for Dionysus.

52
00:03:56,730 --> 00:03:58,021
That's Dionysus.

53
00:03:58,896 --> 00:04:00,480
What do you mean, Dionysus? The--

54
00:04:00,896 --> 00:04:03,146
- Like, the god, Dionysus?
- Yes.

55
00:04:03,855 --> 00:04:05,521
- No way.
- Yes.

56
00:04:12,230 --> 00:04:14,230
- Excuse me, Your Highness?
- Oh.

57
00:04:16,771 --> 00:04:19,230
I think my dad
may be around here somewhere.

58
00:04:22,230 --> 00:04:25,605
I don't know how to ask for him.
I don't-- I don't even know his name.

59
00:04:27,605 --> 00:04:29,813
But I think I should see him. I just...

60
00:04:32,688 --> 00:04:34,230
I think I really need that right now.

61
00:04:36,896 --> 00:04:37,896
Can you help me?

62
00:04:40,938 --> 00:04:41,938
Actually...

63
00:04:45,855 --> 00:04:47,105
I think I can.

64
00:04:49,855 --> 00:04:50,896
Son.

65
00:04:51,646 --> 00:04:53,021
- Dad?
- Yes, Peter.

66
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,771
- It's Percy.
-  Exactly.

67
00:04:54,938 --> 00:04:58,605
Now, before we get to know each other,

68
00:04:58,938 --> 00:05:03,730
there's something very important
I want you to do for me, okay?

69
00:05:05,563 --> 00:05:06,688
In the galley,

70
00:05:06,896 --> 00:05:12,855
there is a bottle
of 1985 Château Haut-Brion.

71
00:05:13,271 --> 00:05:14,563
Will you go fetch that for me?

72
00:05:15,646 --> 00:05:17,355
Is that really all you have to say to me?

73
00:05:17,355 --> 00:05:19,646
- Hey, um, Mr. D, even if Percy was--
-  Uh, uh, uh, bup!

74
00:05:20,063 --> 00:05:21,771
Grover, quiet, please.

75
00:05:21,771 --> 00:05:23,813
This is a nice moment, don't ruin it.

76
00:05:24,063 --> 00:05:25,396
The galley is right down that path.

77
00:05:25,563 --> 00:05:29,271
Grab that bottle and I'll talk to you
about whatever you want.

78
00:05:29,271 --> 00:05:30,771
You know, uh...

79
00:05:32,063 --> 00:05:34,771
you, uh... me, who cares?

80
00:05:56,063 --> 00:05:57,980
- Percy.
- Mr. Brunner?

81
00:05:58,688 --> 00:06:01,813
Uh, Mr. Brunner's real name is Chiron.

82
00:06:02,355 --> 00:06:06,146
Camp activities director,
immortal trainer of heroes, he is--

83
00:06:06,146 --> 00:06:08,438
Grover, thank you. I'll take it from here.

84
00:06:09,438 --> 00:06:12,438
Oh, Percy, this must be a lot
for you to process.

85
00:06:12,605 --> 00:06:15,771
Oh, no. It's-- it's fine.
I mean, you're a horse,

86
00:06:16,355 --> 00:06:18,855
my father won't talk to me
unless I get him a drink.

87
00:06:18,855 --> 00:06:20,146
Well, this all seems totally normal

88
00:06:20,146 --> 00:06:22,188
- and reasonable.
- Oh, no, no, no. No.

89
00:06:23,063 --> 00:06:24,521
Mr. D is not your father.

90
00:06:25,646 --> 00:06:27,480
- I could be.
- Yes, but are you?

91
00:06:28,146 --> 00:06:30,230
Why must you ruin everything?

92
00:06:30,813 --> 00:06:36,271
Mr. D knows that Zeus
has forbidden him from consuming alcohol.

93
00:06:36,605 --> 00:06:39,563
And that demigods are able
to do things for gods

94
00:06:39,563 --> 00:06:41,396
that gods are forbidden
to do for themselves.

95
00:06:41,396 --> 00:06:44,896
Mr. D was taking advantage of that. Hmm?

96
00:06:46,313 --> 00:06:47,355
Eh.

97
00:06:48,230 --> 00:06:49,230
Percy...

98
00:06:50,188 --> 00:06:53,021
walk with me,
and we'll start again. Hm?

99
00:06:55,896 --> 00:06:58,230
Uh, Grover, please give us a moment.

100
00:07:05,563 --> 00:07:07,105
This doesn't feel right.

101
00:07:07,646 --> 00:07:08,813
What, success?

102
00:07:09,688 --> 00:07:11,563
You got the boy to camp alive.

103
00:07:12,688 --> 00:07:13,730
Don't overthink it.

104
00:07:15,271 --> 00:07:17,188
Yeah, but it's...

105
00:07:28,188 --> 00:07:33,021
This is a sacred valley, Percy.
Humans can't see it.

106
00:07:34,355 --> 00:07:35,771
Monsters can't enter it.

107
00:07:37,396 --> 00:07:38,730
The world can't touch it.

108
00:07:40,813 --> 00:07:43,021
Great care was taken to bring you here.

109
00:07:44,271 --> 00:07:45,813
And great sacrifice.

110
00:07:46,438 --> 00:07:47,730
Hey, guys, wait for me!

111
00:07:49,313 --> 00:07:50,938
So, there's something
I gotta tell you.

112
00:07:51,896 --> 00:07:55,396
I lost your pen-sword thingy.

113
00:07:55,896 --> 00:07:57,271
Hopefully, that wasn't your only one.

114
00:07:57,646 --> 00:07:58,896
Check your pocket.

115
00:07:59,271 --> 00:08:02,938
No, I've-- I lost it the other night,
on the hill.

116
00:08:03,271 --> 00:08:04,438
Check your pocket.

117
00:08:08,938 --> 00:08:13,563
Unless you surrender it,
it will always find its way back to you.

118
00:08:14,230 --> 00:08:19,480
Magical objects don't obey
the physical laws of the ordinary world.

119
00:08:19,896 --> 00:08:24,730
Your pen, my wheelchair,
they're all a part of your father's world,

120
00:08:25,230 --> 00:08:26,355
as are you now.

121
00:08:31,646 --> 00:08:33,063
I have something to show you.

122
00:08:40,146 --> 00:08:43,938
Twelve cabins, for twelve Olympian gods.

123
00:08:46,438 --> 00:08:51,355
Each cabin is home
to the children that god has claimed.

124
00:08:53,355 --> 00:08:54,480
Great. Which one am I?

125
00:08:57,355 --> 00:08:59,021
You haven't been claimed, Percy.

126
00:08:59,688 --> 00:09:01,480
Well, when do I get claimed?

127
00:09:01,730 --> 00:09:05,105
Well, the gods reveal their design
in their own time, not before.

128
00:09:05,855 --> 00:09:08,980
Your father might claim you tomorrow,
it might be next week,

129
00:09:09,355 --> 00:09:10,938
- it might be--
- Never.

130
00:09:14,730 --> 00:09:17,355
Even now, he still wants
nothing to do with me.

131
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:21,896
What am I even doing here?
There's no place for me here.

132
00:09:22,355 --> 00:09:23,730
There is a place for you.

133
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:25,980
Here...

134
00:09:29,438 --> 00:09:31,313
Hermes, god of travelers.

135
00:09:32,188 --> 00:09:37,396
His cabin is home to both
his own children, and the unclaimed.

136
00:09:40,688 --> 00:09:43,021
-  Everyone. Everyone.
- Wait-- wait a minute.

137
00:09:43,313 --> 00:09:44,313
Everyone...

138
00:09:45,396 --> 00:09:46,563
your attention, please.

139
00:09:48,355 --> 00:09:50,730
This is Percy Jackson.

140
00:09:51,521 --> 00:09:53,855
I trust you will see to whatever he needs.

141
00:09:58,313 --> 00:10:00,938
I know you feel powerless,

142
00:10:01,605 --> 00:10:04,938
but you're not.
All will reveal itself in time.

143
00:10:11,813 --> 00:10:13,646
-  It jumped up there!
-  I see it!

144
00:10:41,646 --> 00:10:44,313
That's the kid. I think
he's the one who killed the Minotaur.

145
00:10:49,105 --> 00:10:51,813
Look, if you want to give me
a hard time, just do it tomorrow.

146
00:10:52,771 --> 00:10:53,855
I can't do any more today.

147
00:10:54,730 --> 00:10:56,771
Heard what happened
to you on the hill. And I just...

148
00:10:59,188 --> 00:11:00,730
wanted to say I'm really sorry.

149
00:11:03,313 --> 00:11:05,730
I know what you're going through.
Believe me.

150
00:11:08,188 --> 00:11:09,188
I'm Luke.

151
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:14,480
Percy.

152
00:12:05,105 --> 00:12:06,980
You've been picking at them again.

153
00:12:08,855 --> 00:12:09,855
Yeah.

154
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:12,771
You're too hard on yourself, Grover.

155
00:12:13,730 --> 00:12:14,980
You always have been.

156
00:12:23,355 --> 00:12:24,855
Don't be nervous.

157
00:12:26,896 --> 00:12:28,188
Just be truthful.

158
00:12:30,646 --> 00:12:31,646
Okay.

159
00:12:57,271 --> 00:13:00,605
Mm.

160
00:13:05,521 --> 00:13:07,438
Sooner or later,
you're gonna have to choose.

161
00:13:09,896 --> 00:13:12,938
Sorry to interrupt.
Is now an okay time to talk?

162
00:13:12,938 --> 00:13:14,688
- No!
- Yes, go ahead.

163
00:13:16,896 --> 00:13:18,105
It's Sally Jackson.

164
00:13:19,605 --> 00:13:21,146
I think I know
what really happened to her.

165
00:13:21,521 --> 00:13:23,688
I've never seen a Minotaur
crush a human to death,

166
00:13:23,688 --> 00:13:27,313
but I just... I assume that they'd get
really squishy

167
00:13:27,313 --> 00:13:30,355
or something,
or like... like an old banana, maybe.

168
00:13:30,355 --> 00:13:32,396
- Grover--
- But she evaporated.

169
00:13:33,021 --> 00:13:34,146
Like a monster would.

170
00:13:35,188 --> 00:13:36,855
So, I-- I went to the Cloven Council,

171
00:13:36,855 --> 00:13:39,021
and they had actually heard
of this happening before.

172
00:13:39,521 --> 00:13:41,980
And that, when a mortal
is really close to death,

173
00:13:42,771 --> 00:13:45,063
Hades himself
can actually reach out and--

174
00:13:45,063 --> 00:13:46,771
Yes, we know.

175
00:13:48,813 --> 00:13:52,188
But you haven't told Percy anything yet?

176
00:13:52,605 --> 00:13:56,855
No. No one is gonna tell him anything.

177
00:13:59,355 --> 00:14:01,771
I'm... But doesn't he deserve
to know the truth?

178
00:14:01,896 --> 00:14:07,730
Grover, the truth can be very dangerous
if it isn't handled carefully.

179
00:14:09,271 --> 00:14:10,980
I don't want to lie to him anymore.

180
00:14:11,230 --> 00:14:12,521
Come on.

181
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:16,146
There are powerful forces
at work here, boy.

182
00:14:16,730 --> 00:14:19,230
Forces that have laid waste
to the Earth before,

183
00:14:19,230 --> 00:14:20,813
and are close to doing it again.

184
00:14:21,563 --> 00:14:25,855
So, you don't wanna lie
to your little friend? Too bad.

185
00:14:26,605 --> 00:14:28,521
I suggest you steer clear of him, then.

186
00:14:28,896 --> 00:14:34,855
Because you will say nothing
to him about this. Do you understand?

187
00:15:04,105 --> 00:15:08,396
<i>Ah, he left you here,</i>

188
00:15:08,521 --> 00:15:11,855
<i>left you with nothing.</i>

189
00:15:13,605 --> 00:15:16,230
<i>I know how you feel.</i>

190
00:15:16,813 --> 00:15:21,105
<i>You want what's been taken from you.</i>

191
00:15:21,271 --> 00:15:25,646
<i>- You want justice.</i>

192
00:15:31,646 --> 00:15:32,646
You okay?

193
00:15:33,980 --> 00:15:35,021
Super.

194
00:15:35,855 --> 00:15:37,438
We all have them, you know.

195
00:15:38,438 --> 00:15:41,438
Intense, recurring nightmares.
That's normal here.

196
00:15:42,021 --> 00:15:45,313
And the daydreams, and the ADHD,
and dyslexia.

197
00:15:45,938 --> 00:15:50,105
Demigods just process reality differently
than humans do.

198
00:15:50,438 --> 00:15:52,688
For the first time in your life,
you're just like everyone else.

199
00:15:54,313 --> 00:15:55,396
So are you also...

200
00:15:57,563 --> 00:16:00,105
- Do you not know who your--
-  Am I unclaimed?

201
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:02,438
No, Hermes is my father.

202
00:16:03,646 --> 00:16:05,480
That doesn't matter,
we're all on the same team here.

203
00:16:06,188 --> 00:16:07,730
Why is that okay?

204
00:16:08,605 --> 00:16:11,230
Why do they get to bring us here
to just ignore some of us?

205
00:16:11,688 --> 00:16:14,938
Spend too much time trying to figure out
why the gods do whatever it is they do,

206
00:16:14,938 --> 00:16:16,396
you'll drive yourself crazy.

207
00:16:16,730 --> 00:16:18,938
Sooner you stop worrying about that,
the sooner you can enjoy

208
00:16:18,938 --> 00:16:21,188
what this place actually does offer.

209
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:22,355
And what's that?

210
00:16:23,688 --> 00:16:25,438
- Glory.

211
00:16:25,563 --> 00:16:30,021
Demigods have always fought for glory.
They used to call it <i>kleos.</i>

212
00:16:30,646 --> 00:16:34,188
It's like this stuff
that attaches itself to your name.

213
00:16:34,313 --> 00:16:36,730
Makes it bigger, scarier, more important.

214
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:39,021
People listen closer when you talk,

215
00:16:39,938 --> 00:16:41,605
they work harder to be your friend

216
00:16:42,271 --> 00:16:43,980
and they think twice
about messing with you.

217
00:16:44,646 --> 00:16:45,771
-  Hey!

218
00:16:46,021 --> 00:16:47,188
-  Woah!

219
00:16:47,188 --> 00:16:51,521
Hey. Knock it off, Clarisse.
It's like his first day, come on.

220
00:16:52,855 --> 00:16:57,021
Wait, so this is the kid
who killed the Minotaur. Is that right?

221
00:16:57,563 --> 00:16:58,563
Yeah?

222
00:16:58,563 --> 00:16:59,646
I'll bet.

223
00:17:00,688 --> 00:17:02,230
Look, you want attention
around here, dummy?

224
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:04,105
You better be ready for it when it comes.

225
00:17:10,938 --> 00:17:13,063
- Well, she seems nice.
-  Ares kids.

226
00:17:14,605 --> 00:17:15,938
They come by it honestly.

227
00:17:16,230 --> 00:17:18,146
- Why don't they mess with you?
- They know better.

228
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:19,980
Luke's the strongest swordsman at camp.

229
00:17:22,646 --> 00:17:24,521
So, they leave you alone because "glory?"

230
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:27,771
So if I get glory,
Clarisse wouldn't mess with me either?

231
00:17:28,063 --> 00:17:30,521
- Exactly.
- And people think I'm a big deal?

232
00:17:30,855 --> 00:17:32,063
Well, sorta, but--

233
00:17:32,188 --> 00:17:34,230
And my dad's got no choice
but to claim me.

234
00:17:35,521 --> 00:17:37,855
You can't force the gods to do anything.

235
00:17:38,271 --> 00:17:42,146
Well, yeah, but... it would make it harder
for him to pretend I don't exist, right?

236
00:17:42,938 --> 00:17:44,730
- Maybe.
-  Well, great.

237
00:17:45,146 --> 00:17:46,230
Where do we start?

238
00:17:57,063 --> 00:17:59,355
A good source of glory are feats of skill.

239
00:18:00,230 --> 00:18:01,938
So, we gotta figure out
what you're good at.

240
00:18:03,105 --> 00:18:05,271
I wanna be very clear about this,

241
00:18:06,021 --> 00:18:10,230
I've never done anything like this before,
and it looks super dangerous.

242
00:18:10,563 --> 00:18:13,521
And you never killed
a Minotaur before either, 'til you did.

243
00:18:21,688 --> 00:18:22,730
I wouldn't.

244
00:18:34,813 --> 00:18:36,480
Should I try again?

245
00:18:36,605 --> 00:18:37,813
- No!
- No! No.

246
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:43,563
Come on.

247
00:19:02,021 --> 00:19:03,521
Is there a Greek god of disappointment?

248
00:19:04,813 --> 00:19:06,980
Maybe someone should ask him
if he's missing a kid.

249
00:19:08,021 --> 00:19:11,480
Oizys... but she's a goddess.

250
00:19:11,730 --> 00:19:13,480
And her whole thing
isn't really disappointment,

251
00:19:13,605 --> 00:19:14,896
it's more like failure.

252
00:19:18,938 --> 00:19:22,730
We're gonna find the thing
that you're good at. I know it.

253
00:19:28,063 --> 00:19:29,896
- Our turn.
- Our turn for what?

254
00:19:30,313 --> 00:19:31,521
Burnt offerings.

255
00:19:31,980 --> 00:19:33,230
The gods like the smell,

256
00:19:33,230 --> 00:19:35,146
so it gets their attention
before you say a prayer.

257
00:19:35,563 --> 00:19:37,646
They like the smell of burnt mac & cheese?

258
00:19:37,813 --> 00:19:38,938
They like the smell of begging.

259
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:42,521
You burn what you'll miss the most.

260
00:19:43,021 --> 00:19:45,563
Then they know you really mean
what you're about to say, so they listen.

261
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:14,480
Hi, Mom.

262
00:20:17,271 --> 00:20:21,146
I don't know if I'm doing this right,
I hope you can hear me.

263
00:20:24,563 --> 00:20:25,896
I think you used to hate this.

264
00:20:29,396 --> 00:20:30,855
When the phone would ring

265
00:20:31,813 --> 00:20:34,063
the night after you left me
at a new school.

266
00:20:37,438 --> 00:20:39,563
I'd tell you that the people are awful.

267
00:20:42,313 --> 00:20:43,480
That I wanted to come home.

268
00:20:49,105 --> 00:20:52,063
Well... the good news is...

269
00:20:55,063 --> 00:20:56,355
this isn't that call.

270
00:20:59,438 --> 00:21:01,105
I hope you're sitting down, but...

271
00:21:04,063 --> 00:21:07,438
I think... I've made some friends here.

272
00:21:09,730 --> 00:21:12,480
Like, real friends.

273
00:21:15,063 --> 00:21:16,480
I think they might really like me.

274
00:21:20,146 --> 00:21:21,271
Imagine that.

275
00:21:27,980 --> 00:21:28,980
He isn't here.

276
00:21:31,021 --> 00:21:32,146
My father, he just...

277
00:21:34,188 --> 00:21:35,230
didn't show.

278
00:21:38,563 --> 00:21:43,396
I mean, ignoring me is one thing,
but he doesn't get to ignore you.

279
00:21:46,355 --> 00:21:47,855
I'm gonna make him come down here.

280
00:21:50,646 --> 00:21:52,271
I'm gonna make him see me.

281
00:21:56,730 --> 00:21:58,105
I'm gonna make him see us both.

282
00:22:26,563 --> 00:22:28,938
Hey, guys. Can't sleep, huh?

283
00:22:31,688 --> 00:22:34,563
Every new kid shows up here
and they think they're special.

284
00:22:36,063 --> 00:22:37,230
Do you think you're special?

285
00:22:39,271 --> 00:22:40,355
No.

286
00:22:45,396 --> 00:22:49,021
Tell me you made it all up
about the Minotaur, and I'll let you go.

287
00:22:49,021 --> 00:22:50,313
I didn't make anything up.

288
00:22:53,896 --> 00:22:55,605
Some kids gotta learn the hard way.

289
00:23:41,105 --> 00:23:42,271
I can explain.

290
00:23:42,730 --> 00:23:44,021
No, you can't.

291
00:23:45,146 --> 00:23:46,146
Okay.

292
00:23:48,396 --> 00:23:50,688
- Wait, I know you.
- No, you don't.

293
00:23:51,355 --> 00:23:54,688
Yeah, but you were there.
That night in the infirmary.

294
00:23:56,271 --> 00:23:58,521
Yes. I'm Annabeth.

295
00:23:59,063 --> 00:24:00,688
Are you stalking me, Annabeth?

296
00:24:01,855 --> 00:24:02,896
Yes.

297
00:24:03,521 --> 00:24:04,563
Okay.

298
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:07,480
Why?

299
00:24:09,146 --> 00:24:12,938
Well, I've been waiting to see
if something like this would happen.

300
00:24:13,646 --> 00:24:14,938
So I'd know if you can help me.

301
00:24:16,021 --> 00:24:17,105
Help you do what?

302
00:24:17,980 --> 00:24:19,355
Win Capture the Flag.

303
00:24:28,646 --> 00:24:31,438
You're gonna love this.
Camp-wide mock warfare,

304
00:24:31,438 --> 00:24:32,855
all glory to the victors.

305
00:24:33,813 --> 00:24:36,063
Annabeth's the head counselor
of the Athena cabin.

306
00:24:36,605 --> 00:24:38,313
She's led our team to three straight wins.

307
00:24:38,313 --> 00:24:40,271
Been a long time
since anyone's won a fourth.

308
00:24:40,855 --> 00:24:42,188
She was there in the bathroom.

309
00:24:43,021 --> 00:24:45,438
She said she'd been waiting
for it to happen.

310
00:24:46,896 --> 00:24:50,355
Annabeth sees the world differently.
Always six steps ahead of everyone else.

311
00:24:51,188 --> 00:24:52,271
You should cut her a break.

312
00:24:52,521 --> 00:24:53,855
Whose side are you on, anyway?

313
00:24:54,063 --> 00:24:55,563
Oh, hers, always.

314
00:24:56,438 --> 00:24:57,563
She's my little sister.

315
00:25:01,021 --> 00:25:02,355
Maybe I should back up.

316
00:25:04,688 --> 00:25:06,188
Before camp, I was on the road.

317
00:25:06,563 --> 00:25:08,438
Me and a forbidden kid
I met along the way.

318
00:25:09,105 --> 00:25:10,188
Her name was Thalia.

319
00:25:10,730 --> 00:25:12,271
And what does that mean, forbidden?

320
00:25:12,563 --> 00:25:14,938
A long time ago,
Zeus, Poseidon, and Hades

321
00:25:14,938 --> 00:25:16,855
agreed their children
were becoming too powerful,

322
00:25:16,855 --> 00:25:19,480
so they made a pact
not to father any more.

323
00:25:19,938 --> 00:25:23,646
And it held for a long time,
until Zeus broke that pact.

324
00:25:23,771 --> 00:25:24,938
Until Thalia.

325
00:25:26,730 --> 00:25:29,688
A forbidden kid attracts trouble.
Monsters everywhere,

326
00:25:29,688 --> 00:25:31,980
it's just
a constant battle to stay alive.

327
00:25:33,355 --> 00:25:36,396
One day, we, uh, find
this little girl hiding in an alley.

328
00:25:36,688 --> 00:25:39,230
Annabeth. We were worried
about taking her in,

329
00:25:39,688 --> 00:25:41,313
exposing her to all that danger.

330
00:25:43,188 --> 00:25:45,063
Then we saw her fight.

331
00:25:48,771 --> 00:25:49,813
Thalia didn't make it.

332
00:25:51,855 --> 00:25:52,938
But Annabeth and me...

333
00:25:54,438 --> 00:25:55,438
we did.

334
00:25:56,230 --> 00:25:57,855
And we've been family ever since.

335
00:26:00,355 --> 00:26:03,563
She's been watching me
since I got here. Why?

336
00:26:04,271 --> 00:26:07,771
Annabeth is the strongest warrior in camp.

337
00:26:08,355 --> 00:26:11,355
The only way left to prove herself
is to go on a quest.

338
00:26:12,313 --> 00:26:13,980
And what does this have to do with me?

339
00:26:14,355 --> 00:26:16,313
Chiron's been promising her for years.

340
00:26:16,855 --> 00:26:19,813
One day, a demigod would arrive
who was fated to go on a quest

341
00:26:19,813 --> 00:26:21,313
that even Chiron couldn't prevent.

342
00:26:21,813 --> 00:26:23,230
And when that happened, she could join it.

343
00:26:23,855 --> 00:26:27,855
Every new arrival, Annabeth watches,
looking for a sign they're the one.

344
00:26:28,313 --> 00:26:31,730
Usually, she gives up after a day or two,
but she's still watching you.

345
00:26:32,605 --> 00:26:33,855
Can you ask her to knock it off?

346
00:26:34,396 --> 00:26:37,438
Yeah, sure. But what if she's right?

347
00:26:42,271 --> 00:26:43,271
Heroes...

348
00:26:44,771 --> 00:26:45,771
it's time.

349
00:26:47,688 --> 00:26:50,146
The game begins.

350
00:26:53,355 --> 00:26:57,271
The first team to retrieve
the opposing flag and return it

351
00:26:57,271 --> 00:27:00,146
across the river shall be the victor.

352
00:27:00,855 --> 00:27:05,313
As always,
there will be no maiming and no killing.

353
00:27:06,730 --> 00:27:09,355
I trust these rules will be respected.

354
00:27:11,188 --> 00:27:15,938
Any magical items you may possess,
are permitted as well.

355
00:27:16,980 --> 00:27:19,480
- Every camper who is not injured...
-  It's okay.

356
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:21,146
-  ...has to play.
- Let her rip.

357
00:27:21,521 --> 00:27:23,771
Prisoners may be disarmed...

358
00:27:23,771 --> 00:27:25,230
I still don't even know what my job is.

359
00:27:25,230 --> 00:27:28,230
-  ...but may not be bound or gagged.
- Maybe I won't even need a sword.

360
00:27:28,688 --> 00:27:30,313
Let the games begin.

361
00:27:36,146 --> 00:27:37,188
I'm gonna need a sword.

362
00:27:41,813 --> 00:27:45,396
All right. We have 20 minutes
before the second conch and game-on.

363
00:27:45,521 --> 00:27:47,438
- You know what you're doing?
- Yes, ma'am.

364
00:27:48,063 --> 00:27:49,105
Hey.

365
00:27:49,896 --> 00:27:51,396
Today feel like
a winning kind of day to you?

366
00:27:53,021 --> 00:27:54,230
I'll see you on the other side.

367
00:27:56,105 --> 00:27:58,396
Company! Move out!

368
00:27:58,938 --> 00:27:59,980
<i>Kleos!</i>

369
00:28:00,980 --> 00:28:03,355
Not you, sunshine. You're with me.

370
00:28:07,355 --> 00:28:08,355
Advance!

371
00:28:15,271 --> 00:28:18,230
-  Move ahead!
-  Stay in position!

372
00:28:32,688 --> 00:28:39,438
I'm fine, thanks. But I appreciate you,
you know, standing there silently.

373
00:28:46,605 --> 00:28:51,646
Listen, I-- I get it. Okay.
Y-- You're better at this than me,

374
00:28:52,646 --> 00:28:55,021
but I need this to go well today.

375
00:28:56,313 --> 00:29:00,521
I can't really get into it,
but I need my father to see it go well.

376
00:29:01,688 --> 00:29:04,605
So, if you're gonna expect me
to know how to do something

377
00:29:04,730 --> 00:29:05,980
I don't know how to do...

378
00:29:07,355 --> 00:29:11,563
and I end up falling flat on my face,
I-- I can't really have that right now.

379
00:29:21,563 --> 00:29:24,271
You still don't get where you fit
into all this, do you?

380
00:29:28,396 --> 00:29:29,396
Game on.

381
00:29:32,105 --> 00:29:33,188
Wait, what?

382
00:29:35,563 --> 00:29:36,938
Gift from my mom.

383
00:29:37,521 --> 00:29:38,938
Don't worry, you'll do great.

384
00:29:39,396 --> 00:29:40,980
Do great? Do what great?

385
00:30:09,230 --> 00:30:10,230
We give up.

386
00:30:13,563 --> 00:30:16,063
I wanna move quick.
Straight through the woods to their flag.

387
00:30:16,480 --> 00:30:19,063
Clarisse hunts in those woods
for the first few hours, you know that.

388
00:30:19,313 --> 00:30:21,355
- She's gonna cut us down.
- Annabeth's got a plan.

389
00:30:22,146 --> 00:30:23,146
Percy's on it.

390
00:30:24,438 --> 00:30:28,230
When it's time,
he's gonna be ready. I know it.

391
00:31:18,688 --> 00:31:20,105
Flag's that way. It's not here.

392
00:31:20,688 --> 00:31:21,688
We know.

393
00:31:23,730 --> 00:31:25,105
Yeah, glory's fine.

394
00:31:26,521 --> 00:31:28,021
Revenge is more fun.

395
00:31:42,105 --> 00:31:44,938
No maiming. It's like the one rule.

396
00:31:45,771 --> 00:31:48,271
Yeah, I guess I'll lose
dessert privileges for a while.

397
00:31:49,896 --> 00:31:50,938
I'll live.

398
00:32:12,938 --> 00:32:16,230
I'm actually not interested in maiming
or killing you, believe it or not.

399
00:32:16,813 --> 00:32:19,313
I just want you to admit you're a fraud.

400
00:32:20,105 --> 00:32:21,146
It'd make me feel better.

401
00:32:22,146 --> 00:32:23,355
Are you feeling up to that yet?

402
00:32:25,646 --> 00:32:28,521
Guess that's a no.

403
00:33:04,313 --> 00:33:05,438
Get back!

404
00:33:41,813 --> 00:33:44,563
No!

405
00:33:58,313 --> 00:34:00,105
-  Yeah!

406
00:34:10,688 --> 00:34:11,771
Not bad, hero.

407
00:34:17,438 --> 00:34:18,688
Were you here the whole time?

408
00:34:19,271 --> 00:34:20,271
Yes.

409
00:34:20,605 --> 00:34:22,855
You were here the whole time
and you didn't help me?

410
00:34:24,021 --> 00:34:26,063
- Yes.
- Why?

411
00:34:35,021 --> 00:34:36,063
Listen...

412
00:34:37,480 --> 00:34:38,480
Percy.

413
00:34:40,521 --> 00:34:41,646
- I'm sorry.

414
00:34:44,355 --> 00:34:45,563
What is wrong with you?

415
00:35:06,771 --> 00:35:07,771
I don't understand.

416
00:35:22,896 --> 00:35:24,146
Your dad's calling.

417
00:35:36,938 --> 00:35:39,688
<i>You have been claimed by Poseidon,</i>

418
00:35:40,813 --> 00:35:43,438
<i>Earthshaker, Stormbringer.</i>

419
00:35:44,230 --> 00:35:45,521
<i>Percy Jackson,</i>

420
00:35:46,813 --> 00:35:49,188
<i>son of Poseidon.</i>

421
00:35:54,688 --> 00:35:56,771
<i>As a forbidden child of the Sea God,</i>

422
00:35:57,771 --> 00:36:01,480
<i>you are singular amongst demigods.</i>

423
00:36:02,521 --> 00:36:07,730
<i>And your father's only hope
to prevent the outbreak of war.</i>

424
00:36:09,438 --> 00:36:13,771
For months now,
Zeus and Poseidon have been locked

425
00:36:13,771 --> 00:36:16,021
in a dispute over the master bolt.

426
00:36:16,688 --> 00:36:21,063
The symbol of Zeus's authority,
and it has been stolen.

427
00:36:22,063 --> 00:36:23,771
- Who stole it?
- You did.

428
00:36:24,230 --> 00:36:25,230
What?

429
00:36:25,521 --> 00:36:29,313
Zeus is looking for a thief,
sees a forbidden child

430
00:36:29,521 --> 00:36:33,813
claimed by his jealous brother...
It doesn't look good for you, kid.

431
00:36:34,480 --> 00:36:35,938
I didn't do anything.

432
00:36:36,438 --> 00:36:40,188
Of course, you didn't.
But your father needs your help.

433
00:36:40,480 --> 00:36:43,730
An ultimatum has been given to him by Zeus

434
00:36:43,855 --> 00:36:48,438
that if he doesn't return the bolt
by the summer solstice in one week...

435
00:36:50,938 --> 00:36:52,063
there will be war.

436
00:36:53,271 --> 00:36:55,146
That is your quest.

437
00:36:55,980 --> 00:36:57,855
You must leave immediately.

438
00:36:58,355 --> 00:37:00,855
Leave? Leave for where?

439
00:37:01,105 --> 00:37:03,021
Zeus is king on Olympus

440
00:37:03,521 --> 00:37:06,438
and Poseidon has always resented it, but...

441
00:37:07,396 --> 00:37:11,855
there is a third brother
who has always deeply resented them both.

442
00:37:12,855 --> 00:37:14,480
- It's Hades.
-  Yes.

443
00:37:16,355 --> 00:37:20,396
The bolt is with Hades. In the Underworld.

444
00:37:21,063 --> 00:37:23,646
I know it sounds daunting.

445
00:37:23,938 --> 00:37:27,938
But you won't be alone,
a quest is always undertaken by three.

446
00:37:28,313 --> 00:37:31,771
Great. Good luck finding those guys,
'cause it ain't gonna be me.

447
00:37:31,938 --> 00:37:35,396
Poseidon has claimed you.
This is his will.

448
00:37:35,896 --> 00:37:38,688
Poseidon has ignored me my entire life.

449
00:37:38,855 --> 00:37:41,771
- You are his son.
- I am Sally Jackson's son.

450
00:37:42,063 --> 00:37:43,480
Who's Sally Jackson?

451
00:37:45,855 --> 00:37:49,021
She's the one who cared enough
to call herself my mother.

452
00:37:49,688 --> 00:37:53,188
She's the one who got herself killed,
so that I could be safe here.

453
00:37:53,188 --> 00:37:57,063
The fate of the world
hangs in the balance.

454
00:37:57,521 --> 00:38:00,521
- You will accept this quest!
- I won't!

455
00:38:00,896 --> 00:38:01,938
-  Hey, everybody.
- You--

456
00:38:03,188 --> 00:38:05,396
Grover, now is not the time.

457
00:38:05,521 --> 00:38:07,396
I'm sorry, sir. But I have news.

458
00:38:07,688 --> 00:38:10,146
- Grover...
- Sally Jackson is alive.

459
00:38:12,646 --> 00:38:15,271
It looked like she died,
but it only looked that way.

460
00:38:15,480 --> 00:38:17,355
- Grover.
- Your mother was stolen...

461
00:38:18,313 --> 00:38:19,355
by Hades.

462
00:38:20,480 --> 00:38:23,146
Which means she's with him now,
in the Underworld.

463
00:38:23,855 --> 00:38:25,521
That's where they want
you to go too, isn't it?

464
00:38:32,146 --> 00:38:33,605
If you can find her there...

465
00:38:35,646 --> 00:38:36,980
I think you can bring her back.

466
00:38:49,980 --> 00:38:50,980
When do we leave?

467
00:40:36,396 --> 00:40:37,480
Maia.

468
00:40:48,271 --> 00:40:49,688
<i>It's a pleasure to meet you,</i>

469
00:40:49,688 --> 00:40:51,271
<i>son of Poseidon.</i>

470
00:40:52,563 --> 00:40:53,646
I'm Medusa.

